# Pickleball Auth Source Of Truth

## Law

Do not add page-specific sign-in, create-account, password, or sign-out panels to Pickleball program pages.

League/Open Play cross-module auth flows must resolve to the central Pickleball hub, not to a module-specific League, Open Play, RSVP, invite, or account subpage.

## Required Pattern

- The shared Pickleball profile/account page is the only place for account authentication UI.
- Pages that need a user session must redirect to the shared profile/account page with a `return` target.
- After auth, the user should return to the intended destination and see content, not another auth card. For same-module Open Play flows this may be the original page; for League/Open Play cross-module flows it must be the central hub.
- For League Play or other cross-module profile/account entry points, use `SouthEnd_Pickleball_Hub.html` as the `return` target.
- Treat any `return` target under `../../league-play/` or matching `SouthEnd_League_*.html` as `SouthEnd_Pickleball_Hub.html`.

## Applies To

- League pages under `Programs/Pickleball/league-play/**`.
- Open Play, league, message board, and future Pickleball modules under `Programs/Pickleball/**`.

## Exceptions

- The canonical Pickleball account/profile page and its environment mirrors may own the actual sign-in/create-account UI.
- Firebase auth scripts and auth state checks are allowed when they support redirects, session checks, or signed-in data loading.

## Do Not Reintroduce

- Inline cards titled `Sign in`, `Member access`, or `Create an account or sign in`.
- Email/password forms on module pages.
- Local `Sign out` buttons on module pages unless the page is the shared account/profile page.
- `return=../../league-play/...` or `return=SouthEnd_League_*.html` on Pickleball profile/account links.
